@startuml WoT EU Ping Sequence
' Source: ../NETWORK_PROTOCOL.md §§3-4,8 (prefix parity §3). Pcap: wot_server_ping.pcapng (Oct 2022, 20 req / 19 rep).
' Same LoginInterface as login: ping = ID 2, FIXED 1 B (IDA sub_140242660).
' Wire framing per datagram: [4B prefix][flags 2B LE][Mercury bundle][footers]

title WoT EU — WGPinger handshake (UDP port 20016)
hide footbox

participant Client as "WoT client\n(WGPinger / PingerWorker)"
participant LoginApp as "LoginApp periphery\n(port 20016)"

autonumber

Client -> Client : BigWorld.Pinger.ping([periphery urls])\n(predefined_hosts.py, one PingerWorker\n+ PingReplyHandler per host)
note left : PingReplyHandler ctor (IDA sub_1403973F0):\nseq counter init -1, timeout set\ncallback = setOnPingCallback

Client -> LoginApp : ping req (16 B UDP)\nID=2, ReplyID, nextOff=00 00\nseq=++counter (1 B), reqOff=02 00
note left : flags=01 00 (HAS_REQUESTS)\nsender IDA sub_140397AE0:\nwindow-guarded startRequest(ping)

LoginApp --> Client : ping reply (16 B UDP, current)\nreply len=5: ReplyID echo + seq echo\n(no trailer; 2022 servers appended 2 B)
note right : reply prefix VARIES per packet\n(base 0x1f + request top-bit parity;\nnever assert a constant)\nrequest prefix ignored by server

Client -> Client : measure RTT locally\n(send time vs reply time)\nPingData(value, status)\nLOW<=59 / NORM<=119 ms
note left : reply handler (IDA sub_140397700)\nfires next ping immediately;\ntimeout path (sub_1403976B0)\nresends instead

Client -> LoginApp : ping req (16 B UDP)\nID=2, same ReplyID base\nseq+1, reqOff=02 00

LoginApp --> Client : ping reply (16 B UDP)\nReplyID + seq echo, no trailer\n(tester-measured ~34 ms RTT\non login.p2 Sep 2026)

...repeated per periphery (4 hosts,\n5 samples each in pcap)...
note left : login3.pcapng full sweep: 16 B x5 LoginApp\nx5 samples (:20016, login screen, ~4 min\nbefore login) + 25 B x10 periphery hosts\nx15 (:32810-32817, background after login).\nReplicated Sep 19 (5x16 B LOW ~34 ms to\n.215, immediate login+baseapp): no effect\non EU2 silence — no knock precedes\nstage-1 (first manager contact = 22 B).

footer ping = LoginInterface ID 2 (FIXED, 1 B seq)\nflags LE; displayed ping is client-measured RTT
@enduml
